From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Razoc <razoc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:19:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 40/42] feat(akibot): AMD FSR 3 frame generation (frame
 interpolation swapchain)

AKIBOT_FSRFG=1 (KYTY_FFX_SDK_DIR build, amd_fidelityfx_vk.dll next
to the game; ignored when NVIDIA frame generation is on) replaces the
window's swapchain with AMD's frame interpolation swapchain
(renderer/fsrFrameGen.*): create, images, acquire, present and destroy
go through AMD's replacement functions. At the game's temporal upscale
pass the frame's depth, motion vectors, jitter and camera are handed to
it (configure + prepare dispatch), and it presents one generated frame
between two rendered ones.

AMD requires four distinct queues (game, async compute, present, image
acquire): the device now asks for three more queues of the graphics
family when frame generation is requested. AKIBOT_FSRFG_PROBE=1
reports which swapchain variants the surface accepts (diagnostic).

In-game menu: frame generation adds "AMD FSR 3 (x2)".

Checked in Sky Garden (01.007.000), FSR upscaling + FSR frame
generation, game capped at 60: ~1,100 frames shown per 10 s for ~550
prepared (2.0x), no failure, picture clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
